      },
      "cr": 0.125,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Sensei.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 1/8 as a scholar. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>Advisor to Classroom 2-B / SCHALE Liaison</strong> — Trinity General School (advisor); SCHALE</p><p>Status: Active — newly assigned advisor to Classroom 2-B at Trinity General School; disclosed the class's SCHALE attachment during his first roll call and opened an internal query into the Equestrian liaison security breach</p><p>Sensei is the advisor assigned to Classroom 2-B, and the first adult in this campaign's record to tell the students what they are actually enrolled in. He introduced himself as the glue holding the operation together, ran a roll call, and — when a student asked a direct question — confirmed that the class is attached to SCHALE operations. He is not the students' friend and does not try to be. He is the person who answers the question. His method is volume and posture rather than authority he actually possesses. He defused a student's declaration of lordship by thanking him for his cooperation. He is, on the evidence of one session, a man who has run this room before and expects to run it again.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Dagger</strong> — “Advisor to Classroom 2-B / SCHALE Liaison”</li><li><strong>Silver Tongue</strong> — “He confirmed a diplomatic programme with Canterlot, confirmed it was meant to be quiet, and said that students seeing it meant someone dropped the ball on security protocols.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/sensei</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/sensei</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
